# Curriculum-hub vendor reference material is untracked inside the workspace —
# see demos/oak-curriculum-hub/.gitignore (Oak trademarks/logos and the bundled
# brand toolkit are not openly licensed; the export is re-obtainable via the
# claude-design MCP). Mirrored here at the root because root-level tools
# (prettier and friends) read this file, not the nested workspace .gitignore.
# demo-evidence/ is regenerable tool output (tools/ recreates the capture set
# on demand).
demos/oak-curriculum-hub/claude-design-canonical-export/
demos/oak-curriculum-hub/demo-evidence/

# Unsealed audit canary keys: NEVER in git history (standing owner constraint,
# 2026-07-16). Mechanical enforcement added after PR #404, whose commit
# 5612ae244 DID put the two s2 keys into reachable PR history (the PR closed
# unmerged but its ref persists) — those v1 keys are compromised-for-audit
# and re-plant before any canary gate consumes them. Keys live untracked
# beside their consumers and re-plant per audit cycle. Post-reveal
# commit-ability (the r2 reveal step lands the key AFTER scoring) is owned by
# the v2-cycle key work: the reveal convention (a .revealed.json rename or an
# explicit forced add at the reveal step) is decided there, not by widening
# these patterns pre-emptively.
**/canary-key*.json
**/canary-keyset*.json

# Design-system import staging: the downloaded Claude Design studio export
# bundle that seeds / refreshes packages/design/oak-design-system (ADR-213).
